  "body": "When trying to unbind a room alias via the REST API, using this curl command\r\n\r\n```\r\ncurl \"https://matrix.trancendances.fr/_matrix/client/r0/directory/room/%23testcurl%3Amatrix.trancendances.fr?access_token=$AUTH\" -X DELETE -v \r\n```\r\n\r\nI get the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"errcode\": \"M_UNKNOWN\",\r\n  \"error\": \"Internal server error\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `AUTH` variable contains my access token. I tried this with both curl and the official website's [Swagger UI](https://matrix.org/docs/api/client-server/#!/Room_directory/delete_matrix_client_r0_directory_room_roomAlias), both outputing the same error.\r\n\r\nIn the homeserver logs, there's the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2016-12-09 16:10:00,447 - synapse.http.server - 139 - ERROR - DELETE-12691- Failed handle request synapse.http.server._async_render on <synapse.rest.ClientRestResource object at 0x7f5157104110>: <SynapseRequest at 0x7f512d62f5a8 method=DELETE uri=/_matrix/client/r0/directory/room/%23testcurl%3Amatrix.trancendances.fr?access_token=<redacted> clientproto=HTTP/1.1 site=8008>\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/etc/synapse/local/lib/python2.7/site-packages/synapse/http/server.py\", line 116, in wrapped_request_handler\r\n    yield request_handler(self, request, request_metrics)\r\nTypeError: object of type 'NoneType' has no len()\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm using Synapse's latest version (ran the `pip install --upgrade` just now to be sure, restarted then retried, with the same result).",
